From b3dfe57f33093e8c668fcef2f20b5776eb1002b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Rajan <7121943+kvnloo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:30:31 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] chore(gateway): remove dead helpers with no production
 callers

Three gateway-side groups of symbols have no production caller on current
main. Their only references were their own tests.

- gateway/run.py `_start_cron_ticker`: the DEPRECATED shim kept when the
  CronScheduler provider landed (#48275). start_gateway() now runs
  `cron_provider.start` on a SupervisedTickerThread inside
  `_start_gateway_start_cron_and_housekeeping`, and nothing imports the
  shim any more, including hermes_cli/debug.py. Its characterization test
  duplicated `test_inprocess_provider_ticks_and_stops`, so it is dropped.
  The three "cron must not start after an aborted startup" guards in
  test_startup_restart_race.py patched the shim, which start_gateway never
  calls, so their `cron_started is False` assertions could not fail. They
  now patch the real seam, `_start_gateway_start_cron_and_housekeeping`.
  The zh-Hans cron-internals page still named the shim, so it now follows
  the English provider wording.
- gateway/shutdown_forensics.py `context_as_json` and its `json` import:
  production renders the snapshot only through `format_context_for_log`.
  The argv-canary regression (#112459) now asserts on `repr(ctx)`, which
  covers the whole snapshot, instead of going through the dead serializer.
- gateway/platforms/yuanbao_proto.py `PB_MSG_TYPES`, `BIZ_SERVICES`,
  `encode_conn_msg`, `decode_biz_msg`: unused tables and wrappers. The proto
  tests now call `encode_conn_msg_full` / `decode_conn_msg` directly, and
  the fixed-bytes assertions stay unchanged.

No behaviour change. None of the names are in
tests/compat/old_updater_surface.json.

Salvaged from kvnloo/hermes-agent#284, kvnloo/hermes-agent#285 and
kvnloo/hermes-agent#298 (the current-main rebuild of
kvnloo/hermes-agent#115) and rebuilt on current main.

